  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Given the graph of $y=f(x),$ we apply the following transformations in the order given:\n\n1\\. Stretch it by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis\n\n2\\. Translate it up by $2$ units\n\n3\\. Stretch it by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $x$-axis\n\nWhat is the final function expression after applying all the transformations?",
  "worked_solution": "To find the expression, let's apply each of the transformations in turn.\n\n1\\. Stretching the graph of $y=f(x)$ by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis is equivalent to multiplying the function expression by $2.$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=2f(x).\n  $$\n\n2\\. Translating the graph of $y=2f(x)$ up by $2$ units is equivalent to adding $2$ to the function expression. Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=2f(x)+2.\n  $$\n\n3\\. Stretching the graph of $y=2f(x)+2$ by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $x$-axis is equivalent to replacing every instance of $x$ with $\\frac{x}{2}.$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=2f(\\frac{x}{2})+2.\n  $$\n\nTherefore, the final function expression is $y=2f(\\frac{x}{2})+2.$",
